FISCAL NOTE
Senate Bill 223
Committee: Judiciary Sponsor: Senator Linda Coleman-Madison
Analyst: Peter Grogan Date: 04/04/2025
Senate Bill 223 as introduced would allow certain individuals to petition for expungement of
certain Class C and Class D felonies which could increase receipts to the funds that receive a
distribution of administrative filing fees by an undetermined amount dependent upon the
number of individuals that qualify for expungement based on the provisions of this bill.
The current administrative filing fee is $500 and is distributed as follows:
1. $100 to the State General Fund;
2. $75 to the State Judicial Administrative Fund;
3. $50 to the Education Trust Fund;
4. $50 to the Public Safety Fund;
5. $50 to the Fair Trial Tax Fund;
6. $50 to the District Attorney's Office;
7. $50 to the Clerk's Office of the circuit court having jurisdiction over the matter;
8. $50 to the general fund of the state, county, or municipality where the arresting law
enforcement agency is employed; and
9. $25 to the Department of Forensic Sciences.
